<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<chapter xml:id="ch-chapter-Conditional-Probability" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Conditional Probability</title>

  <introduction>
    <p> The problem sets provided here will give you practice with updating probabilities based on prior knowledge that you have about of the scenario or probability experiment. This is called a conditional probability. You will also gain experience in determining when two events' probabilities are conditional versus independent.   </p>

      <p> Each problem set contains two types of problems: interactive exercises and non-interactive ("written") exercises. You will be able to check your answers and get immediate feedback on the interactive portion.
      </p>

  </introduction>

  <!-- include sections -->
